Package: devjam-gpu-x11-xlibre-amdgpu
Version: 1.1-1
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: xserver-xlibre-video-amdgpu | xserver-xorg-video-amdgpu
Recommends: xlibre, devjam-gpu-x11-xlibre-dmabuf
Conflicts: devjam-gpu-x11-xlibre-modesetting
Maintainer: Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>
Description: Use the amdgpu DDX of XLibre on AMD GPUs
 X11 OutputClass section that selects the amdgpu DDX for GPUs on the
 amdgpu kernel driver, with TearFree enabled. This is the alternative
 to devjam-gpu-x11-xlibre-modesetting, which selects the modesetting
 driver for the same GPUs; the two packages cannot be installed
 together. Variable refresh rate and async flips on secondary outputs
 are available through devjam-gpu-x11-xlibre-vrr and
 devjam-gpu-x11-xlibre-asyncflip; atomic mode setting is not supported
 by the amdgpu DDX.
